# full valid-route allowlist above would 404 those legitimate pages.
# To enable hard-404: list every valid client route as `<route> /index.html 200`
# above this line, then uncomment:
#   /*    /404.html    404
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ============================================================================
# SCANNER TRAPS (added 2026-08-21, bandwidth incident)
# Without these, the SPA fallback below answered EVERY unknown URL with a 200 and
# the full ~270KB index.html. That included /wp-admin/setup-config.php - the most
# probed URL on the internet - so botnets scanning for WordPress got a 200 back,
# which reads as "live WordPress here" and invites deeper probing. Each probe cost
# 270KB. These rules return the ~1KB 404 page instead (99.6% less per probe).
#
# SAFE: this is a React SPA. It has no .php routes, no /wp-*, no /.env. None of
# these paths can ever be a legitimate client-side route.
# ============================================================================
/wp-admin/*        /404.html   404
/wp-includes/*     /404.html   404
/wp-content/*      /404.html   404
/wp-login.php      /404.html   404
/xmlrpc.php        /404.html   404
/*.php             /404.html   404
/*.asp             /404.html   404
/*.aspx            /404.html   404
/*.jsp             /404.html   404
/*.cgi             /404.html   404
/.env              /404.html   404
/.env.*            /404.html   404
/.git/*            /404.html   404
/.aws/*            /404.html   404
/config.json       /404.html   404
/phpmyadmin/*      /404.html   404
/phpMyAdmin/*      /404.html   404
/vendor/*          /404.html   404
/cgi-bin/*         /404.html   404
/*.sql             /404.html   404
/*.bak             /404.html   404
/*.map             /404.html   404

# Deleted media (added 2026-08-22). The four home-page videos moved to Supabase and
# were removed from this deploy, but bots that already know the old URLs keep asking
# for them - and the SPA fallback below was answering each with the full ~270KB
# index.html. These return the ~1.2KB 404 instead (~2.8 GB/day at the observed rate).
#
# SAFE: Netlify only applies a redirect when NO real file matches the path (these are
# not forced with `!`). The nine .mp4 files still hosted here - adapt-or-die,
# hero-michelangelo-painting, full-animation-scrub and the six service videos - are
# real files in the deploy, so they are served normally and never reach these rules.
/*.mp4             /404.html   404
/*.webm            /404.html   404
/*.mov             /404.html   404

# SPA fallback - serve the app shell for client-side routes (keep last):
/*    /index.html   200
